(Report 6: Overnight MT5 Forward Test And Price Feed Mismatch) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Report date: 2026-06-03) Tj T*
(Market: Gold) Tj T*
(Analysis symbol used during run: GC=F) Tj T*
(Broker execution symbol: XAUUSD.vx) Tj T*
(Run directory: C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.tradingagents\\sessions\\2026-06-02-overnight-b-plus) Tj T*
(Run type: MT5 forward test with deterministic engine decisions and B+ enabled) Tj T*
(Run window observed in logs: 2026-06-02 15:04 to 23:13 New York time) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Executive Summary) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The overnight forward test was successful as a systems test, but it was not a valid execution-) Tj T*
(quality test because the analysis price feed and broker execution price feed were not the same) Tj T*
(instrument.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The bot ran, generated fresh telemetry, detected tradeable A+ setups, built MT5 requests,) Tj T*
(placed three pending orders, monitored them, and cancelled them after the activation window) Tj T*
(expired. There were no broker rejections and the account ended flat with no open orders or) Tj T*
(positions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The reason the trades did not fill is now clear: the engine calculated Gold entries from Yahoo) Tj T*
(GC=F, then sent those raw prices to MT5 for XAUUSD.vx. At the moments of order placement, the) Tj T*
(proposed entries were about 24 to 41 points away from the live MT5 quote. With a 10-minute) Tj T*
(activation window, those orders were very unlikely to trigger.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This means the main bug is not MT5 connectivity, not auto-trading permission, and not the) Tj T*
(order type logic. The main bug is the live execution data basis.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
