() Tj T*
(7. What Worked) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The following parts of the system behaved correctly:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Fresh telemetry session isolation worked.) Tj T*
(- Duplicate processed-candle checks no longer inflated the summary.) Tj T*
(- MT5 connection and account verification worked.) Tj T*
(- The broker accepted pending orders.) Tj T*
(- Active trade monitoring worked.) Tj T*
(- Stale pending order cancellation worked.) Tj T*
(- B+ grading did not accidentally overtrade.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This means the execution framework is close. The next blocker is feeding the engine with the) Tj T*
(same price source used for execution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. What Must Change Before The Next Overnight Run) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The live MT5 runner should stop using GC=F as the execution analysis feed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The safer design is:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Fetch XAUUSD.vx candles directly from MT5.) Tj T*
(2. Build the same 15m, 30m, 1h, 4h, and daily snapshot the deterministic engine already) Tj T*
(expects.) Tj T*
(3. Run the same engine against that MT5 snapshot.) Tj T*
(4. Place orders only when the proposed entry is near the current MT5 bid/ask.) Tj T*
(5. Keep GC=F only for non-execution reports or separate comparison research.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The order type logic does not need to be the first fix. It already selected stop or limit) Tj T*
(pending orders based on the live quote. The bigger issue is that the entry price itself came) Tj T*
(from the wrong market.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(9. Recommended Next Test) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After implementing the MT5-native data feed:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Run broker-probe and confirm the account, server, and XAUUSD.vx quote.) Tj T*
(2. Run one engine cycle only.) Tj T*
(3. Confirm the engine payload says the data source is MT5.) Tj T*
(4. Confirm proposal symbol, broker_symbol, and MT5 symbol all point to XAUUSD.vx.) Tj T*
(5. Confirm proposed entry is within the configured maximum distance from MT5 bid/ask.) Tj T*
(6. Start a new fresh telemetry directory for the next overnight session.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(10. Conclusion) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The bot did not fail because it could not trade. It failed to fill because it traded levels) Tj T*
(calculated from GC=F while executing on XAUUSD.vx.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The next serious overnight test should not begin until the engine is fed by MT5 candles for) Tj T*
(XAUUSD.vx and the executor has a price-distance guard that blocks proposals too far from the) Tj T*
(broker quote.) Tj T*
ET
